Kaplansky's conjectures fail for torsion-free hyperbolic groups in positive characteristic
Copyright 2026 Nidhal Mghirbi and Seth Douglas

The paper builds on preprints of OpenAI's mathematics release, https://github.com/openai/math, in particular
"A Torsion-Free Group Algebra with Zero Divisors" (23 September 2026), "A Torsion-Free Group Algebra That Is Not
Directly Finite" (4 October 2026) and "A Counterexample to Kaplansky's Direct-Finiteness Conjecture in
Characteristic Two" (23 September 2026). In particular:

- the cone-on-graphs construction, the groups and elements of those preprints, and every estimate the paper
  imports from them are OpenAI's work; the paper lists the inputs it uses (Theorem 3.4 and Table 2) and gives a
  sentence-level account of credit (Section 11);
- the signed cancellation and the two-colour model used in Sections 6 and 7 were found first by S. V. Ivanov
  (arXiv:2610.17662) and independently by the authors; Ivanov has precedence.

No OpenAI source text, code or Lean file is redistributed in this repository. OpenAI's material is referenced by
commit and must be obtained from the repository above, under its own terms.
